One thing I discovered:  There are monsters in the game called "Archon"s.
They are mean.  They are nasty.  They eat little girly-man adventurers as
appetizers.

They always have shields of reflection, and they have Sunsword if you haven't
seen it yet.

>blessed rustproof +3 helm of brilliance

Good choice, although not in the top 5.  I generally pick this up when I am
having problems thinking of a wish.

>blessed luckstone

In the gnomish mines.  Don't bother.

>blessed tinning kit

I find this at least moderately often.  Don't wish for this until you've
checked the tool shop in the Gnomish Mines.

>blessed [rustproof] +3 speed boots

Good call.

>blessed rustproof +3 Mjollnir (this works)
>blessed rustproof +3 Vorpal Blade

The Vorpal Blade is wonderful.  Mjollnir I can take or leave.

>blessed magic marker
>blessed wand of polymorph
>blessed +3 water walking boots
>blessed amulet of magical breathing
>etc etc etc.  Other items are much easier to get.

These I either find on my own or don't desire badly enough to wish for.

Now, my latest and greatest secret for wishes, generally my second wish--
after the Vorpal Blade--or my third, after that and the speed boots:

2 blessed spellbooks of create monster

"What?" you say.  "Why would he want to create monsters?"  Well, I'll tell
you.  This spell allows you to create any monster you want.  Too low a level?
Create a wraith.  Missing teleport control?  Create a tengu.  Missing a shield
of reflection?  Create an Archon, after creating several wraiths to get enough
power to live through the experience.  Missing GDSM?  Create grey dragons
until one leaves scales, and then use a scroll of enchant armor.  Lose
telepathy by converting an altar while a priest was watching?  Create a
floating eye.  Lacking strength?  Create some giants.

As you can see, the possibilities are endless.  Admittedly, you have to be at
least powerful enough to kill a wraith before it lets you get completely out
of hand, but once you have that much power and a blessed spellbook of create
monster, you are PRACTICALLY UNSTOPPABLE.  Barring stupid deaths, of course.

